## API Documentation (Core Endpoints)

All routes are mounted under `/api/v1`. There is no public registration endpoint — the platform is admin-managed, and every write route requires a valid admin session.

| Resource | Method & Path | Access |
|---|---|---|
| Auth | `POST /api/v1/auth/login` | Public (rate-limited) |
| Auth | `GET /api/v1/auth/me` | Authenticated |
| Health | `GET /api/v1/health` | Public |
| Categories | `GET /api/v1/categories`, `GET /api/v1/categories/:id` | Public |
| Categories | `POST /api/v1/categories`, `PUT /api/v1/categories/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/categories/:id` | Admin |
| Services | `GET /api/v1/services`, `GET /api/v1/services/:id` | Public |
| Services | `POST /api/v1/services`, `PUT /api/v1/services/:id`, `PUT /api/v1/services/:id/gallery`, `DELETE /api/v1/services/:id` | Admin |
| Products | `GET /api/v1/products`, `GET /api/v1/products/:id` | Public |
| Products | `POST /api/v1/products`, `PUT /api/v1/products/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/products/:id` | Admin |
| Branches | `GET /api/v1/branches`, `GET /api/v1/branches/:id` | Public |
| Branches | `POST /api/v1/branches`, `PUT /api/v1/branches/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/branches/:id` | Admin |
| Blog Posts | `GET /api/v1/blog-posts`, `GET /api/v1/blog-posts/:id` | Public |
| Blog Posts | `POST /api/v1/blog-posts`, `PUT /api/v1/blog-posts/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/blog-posts/:id` | Admin |
| Packages | `GET /api/v1/packages`, `GET /api/v1/packages/:id` | Public |
| Packages | `POST /api/v1/packages`, `PUT /api/v1/packages/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/packages/:id` | Admin |
| Gallery | `GET /api/v1/gallery`, `GET /api/v1/gallery/:id` | Public |
| Gallery | `POST /api/v1/gallery`, `PUT /api/v1/gallery/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/gallery/:id` | Admin |
| Partners | `GET /api/v1/partners`, `GET /api/v1/partners/:id` | Public |
| Partners | `POST /api/v1/partners`, `PUT /api/v1/partners/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/partners/:id` | Admin |
| FAQs | `GET /api/v1/faqs`, `GET /api/v1/faqs/:id` | Public |
| FAQs | `POST /api/v1/faqs`, `PUT /api/v1/faqs/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/faqs/:id` | Admin |
| Site Settings | `GET /api/v1/settings` | Public |
| Site Settings | `PUT /api/v1/settings` | Admin |
| Users | `GET /api/v1/users`, `GET /api/v1/users/:id`, `PUT /api/v1/users/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/users/:id` | Admin |
| Roles | `GET /api/v1/roles`, `POST /api/v1/roles`, `DELETE /api/v1/roles/:id` | Admin |
| Audit Logs | `GET /api/v1/audit`, `GET /api/v1/audit/:id` | Admin |

> Note: bookings, orders, carts, coupons, and customer-facing reviews are not part of the current data model — the API currently focuses on catalog/content management. These may be added in a future iteration.

### Example: Admin Login

**Request**
```http
POST /api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe123!"
}
```

**Response — `200 OK`**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "login_successful",
  "responseAt": "2026-08-12T09:00:00.000Z",
  "data": {
    "user": {
      "_id": "6650f1a2b3c4d5e6f7890123",
      "fullName": "Super Admin",
      "email": "admin@example.com",
      "role": { "name": "Admin" },
      "isActive": true
    },
    "accessToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs...",
    "refreshToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs..."
  }
}
```

Use the returned `accessToken` as a `Bearer` token (see `TOKEN_PREFIX`) on subsequent authenticated requests via the `Authorization` header.

